		{
			dependencies: [
				"3115EAF1F70A613E"
				"2C6BEB5BBE5A91DC"
			]
			description: [
				"Time to upgrade your &3Electric Blast Furnace&r! &6Kanthal&r is the second coil material available, increasing your EBF's operating temperature to 2700K so it can process more advanced materials."
				""
				"&6Kanthal Coils&r are required primarily for producing &6Silicon&r, required for Circuit parts, and &6Titanium&r, used for &5EV&r machines. An &bMV &3Assembler&r is required to produce them, and they require &62x Kanthal Wire&r, &6Aluminium Foil&r, and &9Liquid Copper&r."
				""
				"&2In GTm, using higher-tier coils provides some bonuses to their multiblocks.&r For the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r, running recipes hotter than required can reduce the energy cost and time taken. The &9temperature&r of the EBF depends on the coil used and the voltage it is running at. For Kanthal Coils, this means that recipes you could run with &6Cupronickel Coils&r will save &95%%&r energy."
				""
				"Refer to the coil tooltip and EBF controller tooltip for the other bonuses provided."
			]
			id: "5C78349343BA40D7"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6AAC5C8B746659ED"
				item: "kubejs:moni_quarter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				count: 16L
				id: "00D5958543D7BBE6"
				item: "gtceu:kanthal_coil_block"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -8.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C78349343BA40D7"]
			description: [
				"&6Silicon&r in its solid form is required to produce &6Transistors&r, which are required for &6HV Circuits&r. Notice that the recipe for a &6Silicon Ingot&r calls for &d2,273 K&r. This is why we built &6Kanthal Coils&r earlier - &6Cupronickel Coils&r can't reach that temperature."
				""
				"Directly heating &6Silicon Dust&r you get from Electrolyzing various materials is an option, but a slow and energy-hungry one. An alternative method is to obtain &6Silicon Dioxide Dust&r by repurposing &6Glass&r you're producing, and heating it with &6Carbon Dust&r. This produces &6Silicon Ingots &dover 5x&r faster, with a side of &eCarbon Monoxide&r for use in various chemical processes."
			]
			id: "0002BA59214CE34A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4103CB323F5BA7A1"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5F5C08701D516EA3"
				item: "gtceu:silicon_ingot"
