		{
			dependencies: ["74935A3553451178"]
			description: [
				"&6Empty Spray Cans&r can be filled with the liquid form of any color dye in a &3Canner&r. Once filled, they can dye any dye-able block (such as &6wool&r or &bAE2 &6cables&r) by simply right clicking. Cans alternatively can also be filled with solvent, causing them to un-dye clicked blocks."
				""
				"Hold shift when dyeing blocks to dye multiple connected blocks at once!"
				""
				"In addition to dye-able blocks, &bGregTech&r &6wires&r, &6cables&r, &6machines&r, &6hatches&r and &6buses&r can be dyed."
				""
				"Importantly, dyed &bGT&r hatches/buses behave differently than when undyed. When dyed, they will share their contents with all other hatches/buses on the multi that are dyed the same color or undyed. Hatches/buses of different colors will not share contents. This can be quite helpful when you need to have separate 'groups' of hatches/buses on a multiblock, such as when dealing with different program circuits."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			id: "2C7306C74609E995"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "More than just colors!"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6BE07CD22A1130B1"
				item: "gtceu:empty_spray_can"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Spray Painting"
			x: 10.25d
			y: 4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C78349343BA40D7"]
			description: [
				"A more advanced type of &6Silicon Boule&r, formed by doping the &6Silicon&r crystal lattice with &6Phosphorus&r."
				""
				"These are made in an &3EBF&r with &2Kanthal&r or better coils, and need &2Nitrogen&r for the process. It needs twice as much Silicon as the basic boules, but also results in twice as many doped Silicon Wafers when sliced."
				""
				"Circuit Wafers can be made far more efficiently with these doped Silicon Wafers, but they are also needed for some more advanced types of Circuit Wafers that can't be engraved onto the basic ones."
			]
			id: "349869EBF2D9FAF1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "43A8ED9E9FB6365D"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [{
				id: "50CCF15D11C3B693"
				item: "gtceu:phosphorus_boule"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2Phosphorus Doped Silicon Boule"
			x: -8.0d
			y: -4.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3E42B4AAA6D2A05B"]
			description: [
				"These devices can help you build, swap blocks, destroy massive areas, or even copy-paste regions. You need the blocks you plan to paste in your inventory though; it doesn't make them from nothing."
				""
				"Also important to note is that it is compatible with &esome&r Tile Entities, as opposed to &bBuilding Gadgets&r which is mainly useful with simple blocks."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"A very cool feature of this mod is how you can &8shift-right click&r an inventory with the Portable Spatial Cloner in your offhand and the tool will pull items from the inventory, 'connecting' it to the inventory."
				""
				"For example, if you &8shift-right click&r a chest full of &6Cobblestone&r with the Portable Spatial Cloner in your offhand, the tool will use &6Cobblestone&r from that chest to place blocks."
				""
				"By default, the context menu GUI is bound to &8Left Alt&r."
			]
			id: "31EE6E41F509A8CF"
			subtitle: "This pack has &bSpatial Tools Compatible&r."
			tasks: [{
				id: "24B4E26B05F638D6"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "itemfilters:or"
					tag: {
						items: [
							{
								Count: 1b
								id: "spatialtoolscmp:portable_spatial_storage"
							}
							{
								Count: 1b
								id: "spatialtoolscmp:portable_spatial_cloner"
							}
							{
								Count: 1b
								id: "spatialtoolscmp:portable_spatial_replacer"
							}
						]
					}
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Pocket-sized pocket dimensions"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 0.75d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["61AD3760E271B431"]
			description: [
				"Ores have various means of processing, and eventually you'll use machine pipelines to process ores in specific ways to optimize what byproducts you gain. You can look at the &6Ore Byproduct Page&r of an ore in &bEMI&r, accessed by pressing 'U' on an ore and navigating to the byproduct tab, to see the required route to obtain desired byproducts. "
				""
				"The relevant machines are as follows:"
				""
				"- &3Macerator&r: turns ores into &6Crushed Ores&r, &6Crushed Ores&r into &6Impure Dusts&r, and &6Purified Crushed Ores&r into &6Pure Dusts&r. &eHV&r and above macerators have byproduct slots and gain a chance to get a full pile of byproduct from ores and both types of crushed ores."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"- &3Ore Washer&r: cleans Crushed Ores with &9Water&r, making Purified Crushed Ores&r, and a chance for a full pile of byproduct. Using &9Distilled Water&r makes them go faster. &2You can also perform a simple wash that is similar to Cauldron washing. It is extremely fast, but grants no byproducts.&r"
				""
				"- &3Chemical Bath&r: &2uses Sodium Persulfate or Mercury to purify certain ores, granting a chance to yield a full pile of a byproduct."
				""
				"- &3Centrifuge&r: separates Pure or Impure dusts into the final material, with a chance for a full pile of byproduct."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"- &3Electrolyzer&r: uses power to split compounds into individual elements, sometimes gaining useful byproducts in the process. &2Be warned that certain dusts may be better to directly smelt instead of electrolyze!&r"
				""
				"- &3Thermal Centrifuge&r: not to be confused with the regular Centrifuge. &2Less slow and power-hungry now, but still so. However, it yields a chance for byproduct, and macerating the Centrifuged Ore can grant a special third byproduct."
				""
				"- &3Sifter&r: &2filters high-quality Gems from Purified Crushed gem Ores for an overall higher yield."
				""
				"-&3Electromagnetic Separator&r: filters magnetic metals from certain ores, increasing their yields.&r"
			]
			icon: "gtceu:lv_ore_washer"
			id: "2B7B623879D6E94A"
			tasks: [{
				id: "0B7B0FFB3FEE3F79"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Ore Processing Machines"
			x: -1.25d
			y: -12.5d
		}
